<https://heatflow.world/vocabularies/heat-flow-method/bullard> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Heat-flow value given as the angular coefficient of the linear regression of the thermal resistance vs. temperature data (used when there is a significant variation of thermal conductivity within the depth range over which the temperatures have been measured)"@en .
